Z||000017||RZURCTN||11-19-1999||11:26 PM||||Regarding your "polar tire repair method".  We do something quite similiar here.  I work with large equipment that has to roll on large tires.  When we have a problem getting a bead to seat we spray a little ether (starting fluid) in the bead and lite it up!  I really hate doing it.  Ever see a Tractor tire jump three feet in the air?  Anyways, it gets the job done quick.||||reg||1
Z||000018||dogtired||11-21-1999||01:47 AM||||Patrick:<BR>In reguards to your inquiry about the moths   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Once you get their legs un-crossed! Youve got em licked!<BR>OH THAT was BAD  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>OK now for the tip of the day?<BR>If I remember right we used to wipe brake fluid on the tires to make them shine.<BR>This was before Armor-All. Don't get it on the rims. After several years the surface of the tire would crack. but hay on highpreformance cars you would use them up before that.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
